theory.intro:
A **composite shape** is made by joining or cutting away simple shapes: rectangles, triangles, trapeziums and circle parts. Split it into those simple shapes, find each area, then add or subtract the pieces. Garden beds, floor plans and paths are solved the same way.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.6]
\draw[thick] (0,0)--(10,0)--(10,3)--(4,3)--(4,6)--(0,6)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (4,0)--(4,3);
\node at (2,3) {$A_1$};
\node at (7,1.5) {$A_2$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

facts:
A piece **joined on** is added to the total.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.6]
\draw[thick] (0,0)--(8,0)--(8,5)--(4,8)--(0,5)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (0,5)--(8,5);
\node at (4,2.5) {$A_1$};
\node at (4,6) {$A_2$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A piece **cut out** — a pool, a doorway, the inside of a border — is subtracted.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.6]
\draw[thick] (0,0) rectangle (10,6);
\draw[thick] (3,1.5)--(7,1.5)--(5,4.5)--cycle;
\node at (1.5,4.5) {$A_1$};
\node at (5,2.4) {$A_2$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.question_text:
Calculate the area of this L-shaped floor.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=5mm,y=5mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\draw[thick,black] (0,0)--(8,0)--(8,2)--(3,2)--(3,5)--(0,5)--cycle;
\node[below] at (4,0) {$8\text{ m}$};
\node[right] at (8,1) {$2\text{ m}$};
\node[above] at (1.5,5) {$3\text{ m}$};
\node[left] at (0,2.5) {$5\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.solution_text:
Split the floor into two rectangles. The lower right rectangle has width $8-3=5\text{ m}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=5mm,y=5mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\draw[thick,black] (0,0)--(8,0)--(8,2)--(3,2)--(3,5)--(0,5)--cycle;
\draw[dashed,black] (3,0)--(3,2);
\node at (1.5,2.5) {$A_1$};
\node at (5.5,1) {$A_2$};
\node[below] at (5.5,0) {$5\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{align*}A_1&=3\times5\\&=15\text{ m}^2\end{align*}$
$\begin{align*}A_2&=5\times2\\&=10\text{ m}^2\end{align*}$
$\begin{align*}A&=A_1+A_2\\&=15+10\\&=25\text{ m}^2\end{align*}$

workedExamples.question_text:
A U-shaped floor has an overall width of $12\text{ m}$ and height of $7\text{ m}$. Each side arm is $3\text{ m}$ wide and the bottom strip is $2\text{ m}$ high. Calculate its area.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=4mm,y=4mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\draw[thick,black] (0,0)--(12,0)--(12,7)--(9,7)--(9,2)--(3,2)--(3,7)--(0,7)--cycle;
\node[below] at (6,0) {$12\text{ m}$};
\node[left] at (0,3.5) {$7\text{ m}$};
\node[above] at (1.5,7) {$3\text{ m}$};
\node[above] at (10.5,7) {$3\text{ m}$};
\draw[<->,black] (13,0)--(13,2);
\node[right] at (13,1) {$2\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.solution_text:
Split the floor into a bottom rectangle and two upper arms. Each upper arm has height $7-2=5\text{ m}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=4mm,y=4mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\draw[thick,black] (0,0)--(12,0)--(12,7)--(9,7)--(9,2)--(3,2)--(3,7)--(0,7)--cycle;
\draw[dashed,black] (0,2)--(3,2) (9,2)--(12,2);
\node at (6,1) {$A_1$};
\node at (1.5,4.5) {$A_2$};
\node at (10.5,4.5) {$A_2$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{align*}A_1&=12\times2\\&=24\text{ m}^2\end{align*}$
$\begin{align*}A_2&=3\times5\\&=15\text{ m}^2\end{align*}$
$\begin{align*}A&=A_1+2A_2\\&=24+2(15)\\&=54\text{ m}^2\end{align*}$

